From 4611569435c75ae895dd30cfd67f504ee23605f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 08:49:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Actually implement the flat-forecast fix (zscore_7,
 days_since_price_change, momentum_7_30, cv_7, is_observed_today)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The fix was previously only documented (README.md, ISSUES_FIXED.md) but
never landed in price_model.py/train_forecast_model.py/app.py — the
deployed model artifact was still at the old 5.8% win rate. This commit
implements it for real:

- price_model.py: _safe_ratio/_safe_ratio_scalar, _days_since_price_change,
  _add_derived_signal_features; wired into add_features() and
  _build_serving_row(); all 5 features added to get_feature_columns().
- forecast_recursive()/forecast_recursive_batch(): thread is_observed_today
  through (True for the first real day, False for every synthetic day
  after).
- app.py: load_series()/_load_series_bulk() now derive is_observed_today
  from the pre-ffill daily resample and pass it to /predict and /trends.
- train_forecast_model.py: self-check reconstructs is_observed_today per
  sampled row instead of assuming True.
- Retrained artifact: crop_mandi_win_rate_vs_naive 0.0583 -> 0.4484
  (100/223), matching what the README already claimed. Self-check passed
  200/200. 108 trees (not the degenerate 1-tree case). zscore_7 is now the
  2nd most important feature; arrival_lag_5 appears in the top 12,
  confirming arrival-volume data is finally contributing.

See VERIFICATION_2026-09-10.md for full before/after evidence.
